Indices (0-based): 012345
$s[0]='W', s[1]='B', s[2]='W', s[3]='W', s[4]='W', s[5]='B'$.
Black cells at indices: 1, 5.
1. First uncovered is at index 1.
   Apply interval $[1, 1+3-1] = [1, 3]$.
   This covers indices 1, 2, 3.
   Black cells covered: 1.
   Remaining uncovered black cells: 5.
2. Next uncovered is at index 5.
   Apply interval $[5, 5+3-1] = [5, 7]$.
   This covers indices 5, 6, 7.
   Black cells covered: 5.
   Remaining: none.
Total operations: 2.
Sample output says 2.

